course: dictionary
lesson: 15793
title: Unaltered: staying the same
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unaltered means not changed. It stays the same as it was before. Break the word into pieces: un- means not, and altered means changed. So unaltered is "not changed".
explain: «The scientist kept the water temperature unaltered, so the test was fair.» The clue is kept. If she kept the temperature, she did not let it change. Try your meaning in the sentence: "kept the water temperature not changed" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Grown-ups often say unchanged or the same instead. «The recipe was unaltered from Grandma's book.» The word tells you the recipe is exactly as it was written, with no new ingredients added. Words like kept and original are your clues.
fact: Unaltered means not changed; it stays the same as before.
fact: Un- at the start of a word means "not", so unaltered is altered with "not" in front.
fact: «Unaltered» can also mean kept in its original state.
fact: In science, the control in an experiment stays unaltered so you can compare it with the other tests.
fact: In maths, «the total remains unaltered» means the answer does not change.
exercise: «The coach left the old rules unaltered for the new season.» What does unaltered mean here? | Written in red | *Kept the same | Changed completely | Thrown away
exercise: In a science test, why does the control stay unaltered? | To make the test longer | *To make the test fair so you can compare the results | To make the test easy
exercise: «The old bridge stayed unaltered after the storm.» Find and copy the word that means not changed. | storm | *unaltered | bridge | stayed
test: «Ben said the picture was unaltered after he cleaned it.» What does unaltered mean? | Brighter | Ruined | Painted over | *Not changed
test: Which word means the same as unaltered? | *Unchanged | Moved | Changed | Broken
exam: «The answer was unaltered after she checked the sum again.» Which is the best meaning? | Lost | *Not changed, still the same as before | Added up twice | Changed, but only a little
